FTABIN
FILE= ../data/weirtabs
FILE= ../data/type5.tab
TABLE#=   -1
 
 
 
; Compute the tables for the culvert and roadway for the U of I
; E-W Access Road crossing Lacey Creek.
 
 
;  Table 7009 represents the departure section for the
;  flow through the culvert and over the roadway above the
;  culvert.  The offsets at the limits were taken to be
;  those that are close to OR slightly beyond the limits
;  of the offsets for flow over the roadway in the CULVERT
;  command below.  It should be no surprise that setting
;  these boundaries is subject to some uncertainty!
 
FEQX
TABLE#= 7009 SAVE22 NEWBETAM NOOUT EXTEND
STATION=     0.897
NAVM=0
NSUB    4     0.090     0.069     0.090     0.090
X-SEC 55  AT EXIT OF 66" X 42" ARCH MP THRU ARBORETUM ACCESS RD
;    -164.0     683.8    1                           OVB   13
;    -102.0     677.0    1                           OVB   12
;     -75.0     678.6    1                           OVB   11
;     -17.0     680.1    1                           CLP   10
      -8.0     679.7    1                           TOB    9
      -3.0     675.6    2                           CHP    8
       0.0     675.4    2                           INV    7
       2.0     676.0    2                           CFL    6
       5.0     677.9    3                           CHP    5
      14.3     679.8    4                           TOB    4
      14.3     690.0   -1
;      39.0     680.6    4                           OVB    3
;     197.0     685.0    4                           BIS    2
;     317.0     681.1    4                           TOS    1
;     469.0     687.8   -1                           BIS    2
 
 
;  Table 7010 represents the approach section to the culvert.
;  Note the notation TOB, Top of Bank at the limits of the cross
;  section.  Note the extension at the last point of the cross
;  section to an elevation of 690 feet.  This is a vertical
;  wall and it is the only line segemtn in section 4.
;  FEQUTL will treat it as a frictionless wall because
;  the subsection has no area.  The EXTEND option in
;  the TABLE line will extend the other end of the section
;  to match.  This extension will also be a frictionless
;  wall.
 
FEQX
TABLE#= 7010 SAVE22 NEWBETAM NOOUT EXTEND
STATION=     0.906
NAVM=0
NSUB    4     0.080     0.064     0.080     0.001
X-SEC 53  AT ENT TO 66" X 42" ARCH MP THRU ARBORETUM ACCESS RD
      -7.0     678.7    1                           TOB   11
      -3.0     675.9    2                           CHP   10
      -1.0     676.1    2                           INV    9
       0.0     675.6    2                           CFL    8
       3.0     675.9    3                           CHP    7
       7.0     679.7    4                           TOB    6
       7.0     690.    -1
 
; Here we compute top width, area, conveyance, first moment of
; area, and so forth for the culvert-barrel cross section and
; ask FEQUTL to save the resulting table, TABLE 1001, for later use
; in the CULVERT command.
;
; Corrugated metal products changed their standard sizes
; in 1980.  That means there are two different sets of
; standard sizes depending on when the conduit was
; manufactured.  Sometimes we do not know when the conduit
; was manufactered.  Furthermore, field measurements of
; the span and rise sometimes do not match any of the
; standard sizes.  This may happen for several reasons:
; 1. The field measurements were not made properly.
; 2. The conduit has deformed slightly under the loads
;    in the field or from faulty installation procedures.
; 3. The conduit is a non-standard shape from some unknown
;    source.
;
; As an example the field measurements here indicate that the conduit
; in this case is a 66 by 42 inch arch  metal pipe.  If we
; scan the standard sizes for pre-1980 no such size is listed.
; The closest match is a 65 by 40 arch.  Scanning the standard
; sizes for the post-1980 again shows no such size.   The
; closest match is a 64 by 43 arch.  We have two options:
; take the closest match of a standard size or use the
; span and rise as given and let FEQUTL interpolate between
; standard sizes to define a non-standard size.
 
; In this case we elect to take a post-1980 standard size
; of 64 by 43 and assume that the measurements in the
; field deviate from this because of deformation of the
; conduit and the inaccuracy of measurements.  The standard
; sizes are also subject to manufacturing tolerances.  However,
; handbooks at my disposal only much the existence of
; tolerances but do not give any values for them.
;
 
MULCON
;  A negative table number forces FEQUTL to compute the conveyance
;  for the conduit including any decrease as the water surface
;  approaches the top of the conduit.  Messages about a decrease
;  in conveyance will be issued at each point which represents
;  a decrease as the depth increases.
TABID= -1001  SAVE22  NOOUT
WSLOT= 0.01
HSLOT= 15.0
NPIPES=    1
TYPE:      CMPA
SPAN:      5.33
RISE:      3.58
BOTT:       0.0
ROUG:     0.024
 
 
 
 
CULVERT
TABLE#=  502
TYPE=   13
LABEL=U of I E-W access road
APPROACH SECTION DATA
APPTAB#= 7010
APPELV=    675.6
APPLEN=  5.4
APPLOS= 0.0
APPEXP= 0.0
CULVERT DESCRIPTION
NODEID=YES
SFAC=1.0
 NODE NODENAME  XTAB   STATION ELEVATION
    1 UPSTREAM  1001     40.25    676.1
      DNSTREAM  1001       0.0    675.9
   -1
CULCLS=PIPE
DEPARTURE SECTION DATA
DEPTAB= 7009
DEPELV=    675.4
LOSOPT=MOMENTUM
DISCHARGE COEFFICIENT DATA
KRB=0.0
KWING=0.0
KPROJ=0.0
C46=0.0
TYPE 5 PARAMETERS
RBVALUE= 0.015
BVANGLE= 0.00
WWANGLE= 0.00
LPOVERD= 0.7
TYPE5SBF= 0.75
ROADWAY DESCRIPTION
PLCWTB= 9994
GLCWTB= 9995
PHCWTB= 9996
GHCWTB= 9997
PSUBTB= 9998
GSUBTB= 9999
    OFFSET     CREST     WIDTH  APPROACH SURFACE
    -7.000   679.430     20.00   678.700 GRAVEL
    -3.000   679.413             675.900
    -1.000   679.404             676.100
      .000   679.400             675.600
     3.000   679.412             675.900
     5.68    679.422             678.446 END
HEAD SEQUENCE DEFINITION
NFRAC=   11
POWER=1.5
0.25
0.5
0.75
1.0
1.25
1.5
1.75
2.0
2.5
3.0
3.5
4.0
4.5
5.0
5.5
6.0
6.5
7.0
7.5
8.0
9.0
-1
 
